WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:01.042
How did you start?

00:00:01.042 --> 00:00:05.797
How did you start with the idea of,
you know, I want to farm? Yes?

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:09.217
But then I also want to teach
because those are two different things.

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:13.304
I think the first recognizing
the huge problem

00:00:13.304 --> 00:00:16.307
that we have in Puerto Rico

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.312
There are economic powers also.

00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:22.981
They don't want us to produce more

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:25.984
because if we grow more,
we are going to buy less.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:29.112
How is it
that one of the most fertile regions

00:00:29.112 --> 00:00:32.115
in the world
is in providing for its people?

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:37.037
Thanks to an American law,
the “Jones Act” Most goods entering

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:41.332
Puerto Rico must make a pitstop in Florida
and arrive

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:44.669
on American made, owned and operated
ships.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.254
The result?

00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:52.010
Grocery prices in Puerto
Rico are 25% higher than on the mainland.

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:56.681
And making matters
worse, products leaving Puerto Rico

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:01.519
are also bound by the Jones Act,
inflating prices of their exports,

00:01:01.811 --> 00:01:06.900
making them simply too expensive to
compete with those from other countries.

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:08.985
So what's left?

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:12.113
High prices and little investment
in agriculture.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.365
It's absurd.

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:17.118
Farmers like Ian know this

00:01:17.118 --> 00:01:19.496
and are taking
matters into their own hands.

